78:["$","ol","ol-18",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"use at least three transactions or units of work in an integrations test: one per each arrange, act and assert section."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"your tests should not depend on the state of the database. Your tests should bring that state to the required condition on their own."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"create two collections for unit and integrations, and then disable test parallelization in the collection with the integration test."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"clean up data at the beginning of a test"}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"write the SQL script manually. It’s simpler and gives you more granular control over the deletion process."}],"\n",["$","li","li-5",{"children":"the best way to shorten integration is by extracting technical, non-business-related bits into private methods or helper classes."}],"\n",["$","li","li-6",{"children":"only the most complex or important read operations should be test, disregard the rest."}],"\n",["$","li","li-7",{"children":"do not test repositories directly, only as part of the overarching integration test suite."}],"\n"]}]
